Script: rapidity_graph_s116b.py
Session: kind-pasteur-2026-03-15-S116b

  Rapidity composition: 1/(2a+1) (+) 1/(2b+1) = 1/(2c+1)
  where c = ab/(a+b+1), equivalently (a-c)(b-c) = c(c+1) = 2*T_c

======================================================================
SECTION 1: GEOMETRIC INTERPRETATION -- PRONIC = 2 * TRIANGULAR
======================================================================

  The core identity: (a-c)(b-c) = c(c+1) = 2*T_c
  where T_c = c(c+1)/2 is the c-th triangular number.

  T_c counts the number of PAIRS from a set of c+1 elements:
  T_c = C(c+1, 2) = number of edges in K_{c+1}.

  So the number of rapidity decompositions of interval c is:
  tau(2*T_c)/2 = tau(c(c+1))/2
  = (number of factorizations of twice the c-th triangular number)/2

