======================================================================
SECTION 3: THE RAPIDITY BINARY TREE -- HALVING OPERATION
======================================================================

  The consecutive-pair family: compose(2k, 2k+1) = k
  This is because (2k)(2k+1) / (2k + 2k+1 + 1) = (2k)(2k+1)/(4k+2)
  = (2k)(2k+1) / (2(2k+1)) = k.

  So every node k has exactly two 'children': 2k and 2k+1.
  This creates a PERFECT BINARY TREE!

  THE RAPIDITY TREE (halving structure):

  Level 0:                        1 (1/3)
                                 / \
  Level 1:                 2 (1/5)   3 (1/7)
                          / \         / \
  Level 2:           4 (1/9) 5(1/11) 6(1/13) 7(1/15)
                    / \    / \    / \     / \
  Level 3:         8   9  10  11 12  13  14  15
                  (1/17-1/31)

