  ANCESTRY CHAINS (trace to root via halving):
  Each node n has a unique path to root: n -> floor(n/2) -> ... -> 1
  BUT this is NOT the rapidity composition -- it's the consecutive-pair path.

    1 -> 1
    5 -> 5 -> 2 -> 1
    10 -> 10 -> 5 -> 2 -> 1
    15 -> 15 -> 7 -> 3 -> 1
    20 -> 20 -> 10 -> 5 -> 2 -> 1
    25 -> 25 -> 12 -> 6 -> 3 -> 1
    30 -> 30 -> 15 -> 7 -> 3 -> 1
    42 -> 42 -> 21 -> 10 -> 5 -> 2 -> 1
    50 -> 50 -> 25 -> 12 -> 6 -> 3 -> 1
    63 -> 63 -> 31 -> 15 -> 7 -> 3 -> 1
    100 -> 100 -> 50 -> 25 -> 12 -> 6 -> 3 -> 1

  KEY INSIGHT: The rapidity halving tree IS the binary representation tree!
  Node n sits at level floor(log2(n)), and its binary digits trace the
  path from root: 0=go-left (even child), 1=go-right (odd child).

  Examples:
